      "content": "While some people feel fine after a small amount of caffeine, mixing stimulants like Ritalin and supplemental caffeine can put unnecessary strain on your cardiovascular system. Even a moderate boost can cause jitters, elevated blood pressure, and anxiety, which will actually hinder your studying. For immediate focus, try taking short, structured breaks away from your desk to refresh your mind instead of adding more stimulants.",
      "source": "target",
