      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Stacking caffeine and Ritalin, even in small amounts, significantly increases your risk of overstimulation and adverse cardiac events. It's not just like an extra cup of coffee; it's compounding the stimulant effect on your nervous system. If you are truly concerned about your ability to stay focused, consider trying a structured plan involving short bursts of high-intensity work followed by brief, complete relaxation periods. For any significant changes to your regimen, professional medical advice is the only safe route.",
      "source": "target",
